# UI Framework

Stack: **Next.js 16 App Router** (RSC by default) · **React 19** · **Tailwind CSS v4** · **shadcn-style primitives on Radix UI** · **lucide-react** icons · **sonner** toasts · **next-themes** (light/dark).

## Structure

- `src/app/` — routes grouped by audience: `(admin)`, `(staff)`, `(auth)`. Each group owns a `layout.tsx` that does auth-gating (`getSession` + redirect) and renders a navbar + `<main>`.
- `src/components/ui/` — generic, reusable primitives (Button, Card, Dialog, Input, Badge…). Do not put feature logic here.
- `src/components/` — feature components composed from `ui/` primitives (e.g. `schedule-card.tsx`, navbars).
- `src/lib/` — `utils.ts` (`cn`), context providers, data/query helpers, palettes.
- Page shell: top-level `<div className="space-y-6">`; header row is `flex items-center justify-between` with `h1.text-3xl.font-bold.tracking-tight` + a `text-muted-foreground` subtitle.

## Primitive conventions (match existing files exactly)

- Components are **functions** (not `forwardRef`), typed `React.ComponentProps<"el">` (+ `VariantProps` when using `cva`).
- Always spread `{...props}`, set a `data-slot="<name>"` attribute, and merge classes with `cn(...)` so callers can override via `className`.
- Variants use `class-variance-authority`; expose `xxxVariants` alongside the component. Support `asChild` via `Slot.Root` from `radix-ui` where composition is useful.
- Import Radix as namespaces: `import { Dialog as DialogPrimitive } from "radix-ui"`.

```tsx
function Thing({ className, variant = "default", ...props }: React.ComponentProps<"div"> & VariantProps<typeof thingVariants>) {
  return <div data-slot="thing" className={cn(thingVariants({ variant }), className)} {...props} />
}
```

## Styling rules

- **Only use semantic theme tokens** for chrome: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border`, `bg-primary`, `bg-secondary`, `bg-accent`, `destructive`, `ring`. These are oklch CSS vars in `globals.css` and adapt to dark mode automatically. Never hardcode neutral grays for layout/chrome.
- Raw Tailwind palette colors are allowed **only** for domain data viz: status thresholds (`text-green-600`/`yellow-600`/`red-600`) and class-type tags — and tags must come from `CLASS_TYPE_PALETTE` in `src/lib/class-type-colors.ts`, not ad-hoc.
- Radii via `rounded-md`/`rounded-lg`/`rounded-xl` (driven by `--radius`). Cards: `rounded-xl border shadow-sm`. Spacing: `space-y-6` page, `gap-4`/`gap-6` within.
- Focus state: `focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px]`. Invalid: `aria-invalid:border-destructive`. Keep these on interactive elements.
- Icons: lucide-react, sized `h-4 w-4` (or `h-3 w-3` in badges); buttons auto-size SVGs.
- Mobile-first responsive: stack by default, expand with `sm:`/`lg:` (e.g. `grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`). Nav uses `px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8`.

## Patterns

- Add `"use client"` only when using hooks/handlers/browser APIs; keep pages/layouts as Server Components otherwise.
- User feedback via `toast` from `sonner` (Toaster mounted in root layout). Avoid `alert()`.
- Loading/empty states: centered `text-muted-foreground` message; empty states use a `border border-dashed` panel with a primary CTA.
- Compose, don't fork: build features from `ui/` primitives + `cn` overrides rather than new bespoke styles.
